{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.MagnusOmega2LocalDecomposition","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MagnusOmega2LocalDecomposition","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.Trace","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Ring.Finset","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.trace_rho_commutatorSum_eq_zero_of_commute","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.trace_rho_commutatorSum_eq_zero_of_commute","kind":"theorem","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MagnusOmega2LocalDecomposition.lean#L138-L153","doc":"**The decay endpoint is an EXACT zero (the commutative/1-dim rep).** If the germs pairwise\ncommute — `Commute (A k) (B k)` for every adjacent pair `k`, which holds in *any* 1-dimensional\n(hence commutative) seminormal rep — then the Magnus `Ω₂ = Σ_k ⁅A_k,B_k⁆` is `0`, so the\nsingle-window sum trace `tr(ρ·Ω₂) = 0` identically, for every word `ρ`. In particular the\nmaximal-`b` endpoint of the `tr(ρ_λ Ω₂)` decay, the **sign rep** `λ=(1ⁿ)` (dim 1), and the\n`b=0` **trivial rep** `λ=(n)` (dim 1) both give an exact zero — the decay terminates at a\nprovable zero, not an asymptote (measured in `magnus_extreme_rep_endpoint_probe.py`). General\n`CommRing`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.commutator_mul_left","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.commutator_mul_left","kind":"theorem","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MagnusOmega2LocalDecomposition.lean#L127-L136","doc":"**Leibniz rule for the ring commutator (the telescoping tool).**\n`⁅X·Y, Z⁆ = X·⁅Y,Z⁆ + ⁅X,Z⁆·Y`. Applied to the density `ρ = ∏_i σ_{g_i}` this telescopes:\n`⁅ρ, A_a⁆ = Σ_i (σ_{<i})·⁅σ_{g_i}, A_a⁆·(σ_{>i})`, and `⁅σ_g, A_a⁆ = 0` whenever\n`|g−a| ≥ 2` (the generators far from `a` commute with the germ `A_a`). So only the O(1)\ncrossings *near position a* contribute to `⁅ρ,A_a⁆` — the structural handle that reduces the\nopen Frobenius bound `‖⁅ρ_λ,A_a⁆‖_F = o(√dim)` to a bounded number of *local* commutators\n`⁅σ_g, A_a⁆` (3-strand objects) dressed by word-pieces. General `CommRing`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.trace_rho_commutator_reframe'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.trace_rho_commutator_reframe'","kind":"theorem","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MagnusOmega2LocalDecomposition.lean#L119-L125","doc":"**Reframing onto the other germ (sign partner).** `tr(ρ·⁅A,B⁆) = −tr(⁅ρ,B⁆·A)`. Together\nwith `trace_rho_commutator_reframe` this gives the estimator two handles — the trace is\nsmall when `ρ` nearly commutes with *either* germ. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.trace_rho_commutator_reframe","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.trace_rho_commutator_reframe","kind":"theorem","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MagnusOmega2LocalDecomposition.lean#L106-L117","doc":"**Trace-commutator reframing (the sublinear-bound tool).** The single-window trace can be\nmoved onto the density: `tr(ρ·⁅A,B⁆) = tr(⁅ρ,A⁆·B)`. This localizes the open sublinear\nestimate `|tr(ρ_λ ⁅A_a,A_{a+1}⁆)| = o(dim_λ)` (bean `qou-o6ov`): the whole size of the\nsingle-window trace is controlled by `⁅ρ,A_a⁆`, i.e. by *how nearly the global word `ρ`\ncommutes with the germ `A_a`*. Combined with Cauchy–Schwarz\n`|tr(X·B)| ≤ ‖X‖_F‖B‖_F` (not in this file) it reduces the `o(dim)` claim to a\nFrobenius-norm bound on `⁅ρ,A_a⁆`. General `CommRing`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.trace_rho_weightedLocalSum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.trace_rho_weightedLocalSum","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MagnusOmega2LocalDecomposition.lean#L94-L104","doc":"**Weighted per-window trace decomposition.** With integer/scalar window multiplicities `c k`\n(the probe's `mult(a,a+1)`), `tr(ρ · Σ_k c_k • O_k) = Σ_k c_k · tr(ρ · O_k)`. Instantiated at\n`O_k = ⁅A_a,A_{a+1}⁆` and `c_k = mult` this is exactly the probe's self-check identity\n`2·tr(ρ Ω₂) = Σ mult·tr(ρ ⁅A_a,A_{a+1}⁆)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.trace_rho_localSum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.trace_rho_localSum","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MagnusOmega2LocalDecomposition.lean#L85-L92","doc":"**Per-window trace decomposition (linearity).** The trace of `ρ` against a sum of local\nwindow operators is the sum of the per-window traces:\n`tr(ρ · Σ_k O_k) = Σ_k tr(ρ · O_k)`. This is the algebraic identity the probe's numeric\nself-check confirms; it makes `tr(ρ Ω₂)`'s b-decay attributable window-by-window. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.omega2_reduces_to_adjacent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.omega2_reduces_to_adjacent","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MagnusOmega2LocalDecomposition.lean#L66-L83","doc":"**Ω₂ reduces to adjacent windows.** Sum a family of commutators `⁅fst p, snd p⁆` over a\nfinset `s` of ordered crossing-pairs; if every *non-adjacent* pair commutes, the sum equals the\nsum over the *adjacent* pairs alone. This is the operator identity\n`Σ_{i<j} ⁅A_i,A_j⁆ = Σ_{adjacent} ⁅A_a,A_{a+1}⁆` — far pairs contribute nothing, so `Ω₂` is a\nlattice sum of 3-strand-local windows. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.commutator_eq_zero_of_commute","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.commutator_eq_zero_of_commute","kind":"theorem","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MagnusOmega2LocalDecomposition.lean#L58-L64","doc":"**Far-commutativity reduction core.** A commutator of commuting operators vanishes:\n`Commute A B → A*B − B*A = 0`. For the Magnus germs `A_a = q·(∂_q σ_a)·σ_a⁻¹`, germs at\nCoxeter distance `|a−b| ≥ 2` commute (their generators do), so `⁅A_a,A_b⁆ = 0` — the term\ndrops from `Ω₂`. This is the operator content of the probe's `if |a−b| ≠ 1: continue`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}